            <div xml:id="d1088">

                <pb facs="0971" n="959" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg959"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52 Agrarian Commission/153: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Commissioner, Agrarian Claims
                        Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">El
                                Paso, Texas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-09">June 9, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received June 10—7:58
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference final paragraph Department’s June 8, 2 p.m. Respectfully suggest that
                    because of limited time Department urge immediate and definite authorization be
                    given Serrano to negotiate final global settlement without raising any
                    controversial legal questions, particularly that arising in claims of
                    stockholders of Mexican companies which is of course one of the principal
                    reasons of suggested global settlement. Also request telegraphic advice as soon
                    as Serrano has been given such authority and is prepared to take final and
                    definite action. Air mail<anchor n="16" xml:id="d1088-f1"/> follows concerning
                    inclusion of claims referred to in third sentence of fourth paragraph of
                    telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
